  "behavior": [
    "Clear stale ostream and default stderr C-stream errors before each new file notice; check insertion and flushing.",
    "Retain failed line-mode notices until restoration; later notices receive fresh normal attempts. No EAGAIN retry loop.",
    "Share normal/emergency delivery with an allocation-free function-pointer-backed default sink; preserve full Unicode paths and original exceptions.",
    "A fully constructed RAII member owns terminal resources before startup can throw. Native adapters enable deterministic partial-acquisition tests.",
    "Keep ordinary diagnostic semantics and live/cleanup/file replay order, including independent drains and one emergency attempt per released notice.",
    "Share allocation-free UTF-8 decoding without changing malformed-prefix replacement or canonical JSON equality.",
    "Escape U+00AD, U+200B, U+2060-U+2064, U+206A-U+206F, U+FEFF in addition to the existing unsafe set; preserve joiners, variation selectors, multilingual paths and emoji.",
    "Link SQLite preparation interception exclusively into the host benchmark and publication-fault executable."
  ],
